From f82f03e401b9351c04766fa0dcc76ae239a6adcc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:10:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test(baseline): a JSON Schema per snapshot kind; every
 committed snapshot checked against its kind

Generated from the model types with schemars: known_defects, round_trip,
writer, shed, validate (docs/baseline/schemas/, regenerate with
UPDATE_SCHEMAS=1 cargo test -p toolpath-goldens --test schemas).
Hand-written: formats, validate_transforms, opencode_db (bodies built
with json!), document (the base schema plus the v1.1.0 kind, checked the
way path p validate checks it) and recording provenance. No schema, with
the reason: projection (harness-native) and ir (ConversationView has
none; qualifier concern baa7a7b5).

tests/schemas.rs: generated schemas current; every committed snapshot
validates against its kind; every recording's provenance validates. A
snapshot with a broken shape fails by name (negative control run by hand).
All committed snapshots pass. Record: pr/41-baseline-schemas.md.
